<section>
  <grid spacing="medium">
    <grid-item colspan="25" vertical-align="center">
      <p role="eyebrow">Evidence bearing 02</p>
      <h2>Relic light on every horizon</h2>
      <display font-size="48pt">≈380,000 years</display>
      <p>After the hot beginning, the universe became transparent enough for light to travel freely. Expansion has since cooled that light into microwaves.</p>
      <hr horizontalAlign="left" width="xs" thickness="md" color="accent"/>
      <h4>Cosmic microwave background</h4>
      <p>Relic light from the early universe—seen across the sky, not pointing back to one central blast port.</p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="35" padding="0">
      <ai-image background="true" image-style="celestial-copperplate" aspect-ratio="landscape" prompt="Digitally illustrated copperplate celestial engraving of relic microwave light arriving from every horizon, an observer's scientific instrument at the lower edge surrounded by a continuous sphere of faint mottled radiation, abyssal-blue field, crisp ivory coordinate arcs, oxidized-brass fittings, cyan glow with sparse coral signal flecks, no center point, no explosion, no chart labels or lettering"></ai-image>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>